    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d606">

                <pb facs="0905" n="1413" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/9–1748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in the United Kingdom
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-18T14:00:00-04:00">September 18,
                            1948—2 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3690. For Ambassador Douglas.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>We agree (para 2 Embtel 4153, Sept. 17)
                        Bernadotte report may be published as early as Sept. 20.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>Secretary will make decision in Paris (para 6). Confidentially our present
                        inclination is to make statement there before British.</item>
                    <label>(3)</label>
                    <item>Sec plans leave Washington early afternoon Sept. 19, arriving in Paris
                        Sept. 20.</item>
                    <label>(4)</label>
                    <item>We are preparing US statement (para 8) which Sec will probably take with
                        him for discussion with GADel Paris
                        following arrival.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Sent London, repeated Paris for Jessup and McClintock in reply Delga 59, Sept. 18.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d606-f1"
                    />
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d606-f1" n="1" xml:id="d606-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; Mr. McClintock, in this message to Messrs. Lovett and Rusk,
                    recommended strongly that there be no ten-day delay in publishing the Bernadotte
                    report and concluded: “Bernadotte’s death will give maximum weight to
                    recommendations in his report. I feel that if report is issued promptly, there
                    will still be sufficient time for diplomatic preparation, particularly since
                    British already contemplate swift action.” (501.BB/9–1848)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
